    "https://careers.callutheran.edu/postings/13717": {
      "title": "Administrative Assistant - Performing Arts & Humanities",
      "description": "Cal Lutheran Employment Opportunities | Administrative Assistant - Performing Arts &amp; Humanities Skip to Main Content Careers at Cal Lutheran Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Interest Cards California Lutheran University Pacific Lutheran Theological Seminary Human Resources E-verify Employer Benefits Maps & Directions Student Employment Office Annual Security Report - All Campuses Administrative Assistant - Performing Arts & Humanities Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Position Title Administrative Assistant - Performing Arts & Humanities Position Category Staff (Non-Exempt) FLSA Non-exempt FTE 1.0 Location Thousand Oaks University Background The mission of California Lutheran University is to educate leaders for a global society who are strong in character and judgment, confident in their identity and vocation, and committed to service and justice. Founded in 1959 in beautiful Ventura County, the university has an enrollment of about 4,000 undergraduate and graduate students who come from across the nation and around the world from a diversity of backgrounds, cultures and faiths. As a federally recognized Hispanic-Serving Institution, Cal Lutheran is looking for candidates with a dedication to and success in working in diverse communities. The university is committed to an inclusive learning and work environment that values individual differences and respects each person’s dignity. Basic Function Under the direction of the College Services Manager ( CSM ), the Administrative Assistant performs a variety of responsible administrative and support functions to assist faculty in delivering quality academic programs. The position provides administrative support to academic departments within the Humanities and Creative and Performing Arts divisions of the College of Arts & Sciences. Specific departmental assignments and responsibilities may vary based on the operational needs and priorities of the College. Representative Duties Faculty & Department Support Provide administrative support to assigned academic departments, including Humanities, Visual Arts, Theatre & Dance, and Film & Television faculty and department chairs. E Coordinate faculty communications, scheduling requests, and departmental operations. E Maintain faculty directories, office hours, syllabi collection, adjunct schedules, and departmental records. E Maintain departmental academic records and assist with student-related administrative processes, including scholarship applications, internships, and program records, as assigned. E Organize adjunct office spaces and support onboarding of new faculty and lecturers. E As needed, support department meetings and divisional meetings through scheduling, agendas, minutes, and logistics. E Budget, Purchasing & Financial Support Process purchase requisitions, requests for payment (RFPs), reimbursements, contracts, and purchasing documentation. E As needed, track department budgets and expenditures and assist chairs with budget monitoring. E Complete bi-monthly reconciliations and maintain organized financial records. Coordinate with vendors and follow up on invoices, payments, and purchase orders. Maintain supply inventories and coordinate office and instructional supply orders. E Building & Facilities Support Serve as an administrative support contact for assigned departmental facilities, which may include: William Rolland Art Center ( WRAC ) Soiland Humanities Building Film spaces within SBET Black Box Theatre Preus-Brandt Forum Building & Facilities Responsibilities Include: Submit and track facilities requests, maintenance issues, and work orders. Coordinate room reservations and event scheduling. E Assist with office moves, key requests, signage, and directory updates. E Coordinate with Facilities, ITS , Media Services, and Campus Safety as needed. E Monitor shared equipment, printers, and operational readiness of supported spaces. E Visual & Performing Arts, Events, Exhibitions & Performances Provide specialized administrative support for departmental academic and co-curricular activities, including performances, rehearsals, exhibitions, student showcases, auditions, juries, tours, and other program-specific activities, as assigned. E Support planning and coordination of performances, screenings, exhibitions, receptions, lectures, and special events. E Coordinate event logistics, including room scheduling, setup requests, hospitality, signage, and communications. E Assist with gallery exhibitions and receptions, theatre productions, student showcases, Film & Television events, and other Visual and Performing Arts activities, as assigned. E Support departmental ticketing and box office operations, including online ticketing systems, ticket sales, and related administrative coordination, as assigned. E Coordinate with Marketing & Communications regarding event promotion, publicity materials, and related support. E Student & Office Operations Provide front-line customer service to students, faculty, guests, and visitors. Maintain organized records, filing systems, and confidential documents. Manage mail distribution, office supply inventory, and general office operations. E Additional Duties Serve as backup support within the COAS administrative team as needed. Support accreditation, assessment, and institutional initiatives as assigned. Perform related duties as assigned. E = Essential Duties Knowledge Of Organization, policies, procedures, and operations of the College of Arts & Sciences and assigned academic departments, including Humanities and Creative and Performing Arts. Modern office practices, procedures, equipment, and administrative systems. Organizational methods, recordkeeping techniques, and the ability to manage multiple priorities and support multiple departments and facilities. Standard office software, database systems, data entry techniques, and Microsoft Office and Mac applications. Correct English usage, grammar, spelling, punctuation, and vocabulary. Effective oral and written communication, customer service, and public relations techniques. Interpersonal skills using tact, patience, courtesy, and professionalism when working with faculty, students, staff, and campus partners. Telephone techniques, professional correspondence, and office etiquette. Event planning, scheduling, coordination, and operational logistics for academic programs, performances, exhibitions, and departmental activities. Department-specific terminology, practices, and operational needs, including those associated with Visual and Performing Arts programs. Collaborative work practices and effective coordination with multiple departments and University offices. Ability To Perform a variety of administrative and clerical duties in support of multiple academic departments. Organize, coordinate, and prioritize office activities while managing multiple tasks, deadlines, and interruptions. Operate standard office equipment, computers, and administrative software systems. Maintain accurate records, spreadsheets, databases, and confidential information. Prepare correspondence, reports, and other written materials with accuracy and attention to detail. Gather and organize information, perform basic calculations, and assist with financial tracking and reconciliation. Communicate clearly and professionally, both orally and in writing, and provide excellent customer service. Learn, interpret, and apply University policies, procedures, and regulations. Coordinate meetings, events, performances, exhibitions, and related departmental activities. Exercise independent judgment, problem-solving skills, and discretion within established guidelines. Establish and maintain effective working relationships with faculty, students, staff, and campus partners. Identify opportunities to improve administrative processes and office operations. Adapt to changing priorities and departmental needs while working independently and collaboratively. Understand and follow oral and written instructions. Minimum Qualifications Any combination equivalent to: two years of college-level coursework and two year of administrative support experience. Preferred Qualifications Prior experience as an administrative assistant in a non-profit, corporate, higher education, or in a performing/creative arts setting. Strong organizational and communication skills. Licenses and other requirements None Physical Abilities Detect to understand appropriate written correspondence; operate a computer and other office productivity machinery, such as a calculator, copy machine, and computer printer; communicate to exchange information in person, in writing, on the telephone and by email; stationary position for extended periods of time; move or transport light objects; position self to store and/or retrieve files Environment Busy office environment; subject to frequent interruptions. Hiring Range $21.00-$23.00 Posting Detail Information Posting Number Staff005732022 Number of Vacancies 1 Desired Start Date 11/23/2026 Position End Date Open Date 10/23/2026 Close Date 11/08/2026 Open Until Filled No Application Procedure/Special Instructions Statement California Lutheran University is committed to providing equal opportunity in employment for all persons, regardless of race, religious creed, color, national origin, ancestry, physical disability, mental disability, medical condition, marital status, sex, age, sexual orientation, genetic information, gender, gender identity or expression, or any other basis protected by applicable law. No person shall be excluded from participation in, be denied the benefits of, or be subjected to discrimination in any program, activity or facility of the University on the basis of these factors in a manner consistent with applicable federal and state laws, regulations, ordinances, orders and rules, and University’s policies, procedures, and processes. Upon request, reasonable accommodations in the application process can be provided to individuals with qualifying disabilities. Please contact the Human Resources Department for further information or to request an accommodation. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Optional Documents Human Resources California Lutheran University 60 W. Olsen Rd. #1100 Thousand Oaks, CA 91360 Office (805) 493-3185 Fax (805) 493-3655 California Lutheran University is an Equal Opportunity Employer To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://careers.callutheran.edu/postings/13248": {
      "title": "Adjunct Pool - Psy.D - Clinical Psychology Program",
      "description": "Cal Lutheran Employment Opportunities | Adjunct Pool - Psy.D - Clinical Psychology Program Skip to Main Content Careers at Cal Lutheran Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Applicant Interest Cards California Lutheran University Pacific Lutheran Theological Seminary Human Resources E-verify Employer Benefits Maps & Directions Student Employment Office Annual Security Report - All Campuses Adjunct Pool - Psy.D - Clinical Psychology Program Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Position Title Adjunct Pool - Psy.D - Clinical Psychology Program Position Category Adjunct FLSA Exempt Position Status Adjunct Location Oxnard University Background Cal Lutheran is a Hispanic-Serving Institution ( HSI ) and McNair Institution, and we are looking for candidates with a demonstrated commitment to and success working in diverse, multi- cultural and multi-racial communities, particularly in mentoring African American, Latinx, and Native American students. Cal Lutheran encourages applicants from all faiths or none, and advocates for justice and fairness for all people. We are an accredited, private, comprehensive university dedicated to engaging students in critical inquiry and educating leaders for a global society. Cal Lutheran is home to more than 3,100 undergraduate and graduate students who come from 67 countries and represent a variety of faiths. 52% of Cal Lutheran students are from underrepresented groups, and 43% of freshmen are first generation students. Cal Lutheran Faculty are 32% people of color. The mission of the University is to educate leaders for a global society who are strong in character and judgment, confident in their identity and vocation, and committed to service and justice. Basic Function Under the direction of the Dean, Department Chair or Program Director, the Adjunct Faculty Member is responsible for providing academic instruction to students for the assigned graduate courses. Representative Duties Provide academic instruction to students through lecture, lab, or performance courses; assess and develop cognitive abilities, communication skills, and higher order thinking skills among students through appropriate assignments and activities in one-on-one, classroom, and distance mediated instructional settings. E Advise and instruct students regarding programs of study, other institutions of higher education, lifelong learning resources, and effective study skills; refer students to support services, programs, resources, and other professionals as appropriate. E Observe and evaluate student performance in meeting course objectives and student learning outcomes through assignments, projects, discussions, and examinations; provide feedback in a timely manner to student inquiries in class, online, or during established consultation office hours. E Plan and organize instruction according to approved course outlines and student learning outcomes to maximize student learning in alignment with department, and university mission/goals; implement the student performance objectives as listed on the official course outline of record. E Maintain current, accurate records of course enrollment, attendance, student academic progress, course curriculum, and student learning outcomes; prepare and submit data and reports related to course and student progress in a timely manner. E Evaluate and select instructional materials such as textbooks, manuals, software, and tools in collaboration, as appropriate, with discipline faculty; order instructional materials according to campus bookstore procedure to ensure timely delivery. E Performs related duties as assigned. E=Essential Duties Knowledge Of Current theory and practice within the subject discipline Principles and best practices of effective teaching Ability To Demonstrate a thorough and accurate knowledge in the subject field or discipline Deliver course curricula in various learning styles Exhibit sensitivity to and understanding of the diverse academic, social, economic, cultural, and ethnic backgrounds of University students. Exhibit sensitivity to and understanding of the needs of students with disabilities. Integrate current and emerging instructional delivery technologies into the learning process to enhance teaching and the educational experience Maintain professional standards that protect student confidentiality Communicate effectively, both orally and in writing using tact, patience, and courtesy Minimum Qualifications Possession of a master’s degree from a graduate institution of recognized standing or equivalent experience and professional recognition. Preferred Qualifications None Licenses and other requirements None Physical Abilities Manual dexterity of hands and fingers to operate office equipment; speaking to exchange information, provide instruction and make presentations; sitting or standing for extended periods of time; pushing, pulling or lifting light objects; bending and reaching to store and/or retrieve files. Working Environment Indoor classroom environment; subject to visiting a variety of classroom sites on campus. Hiring Range $32-$34.50 an hour Posting Detail Information Posting Number Adjunct000392019 Number of Vacancies Dependent upon enrollment Desired Start Date Position End Date Open Date 06/01/2020 Close Date 05/31/2027 Open Until Filled No Application Procedure/Special Instructions The Cal Lutheran Graduate School of Psychology invites applications for part-time adjunct faculty positions for the Fall and Spring semesters. New applications will be reviewed on an ongoing basis. Applicants will be contacted by the Department Chair based upon need and applicant qualifications. Statement California Lutheran University is an accredited, private, comprehensive university located midway between Santa Barbara and Los Angeles. Cal Lutheran is home to more than 3,100 undergraduate and graduate students who come from more than 66 countries and represent a wide variety of faiths. 48% of Cal Lutheran students are international students or from underrepresented groups, and over 40% of first-time freshmen are first generation students. Over 45% of graduate students in the School of Management are international students. The University encourages candidates who will contribute to the cultural diversity of Cal Lutheran to apply. Additional information may be found at www.callutheran.edu. All offers will be contingent upon the completion of a successful background check. California Lutheran University is committed to providing equal opportunity in employment for all persons, regardless of race, religious creed, color, national origin, ancestry, physical disability, mental disability, medical condition, marital status, sex, age, sexual orientation, genetic information, gender, gender identity or expression, or any other basis protected by applicable law. No person shall be excluded from participation in, be denied the benefits of, or be subjected to discrimination in any program, activity or facility of the University on the basis of these factors in a manner consistent with applicable federal and state laws, regulations, ordinances, orders and rules, and University’s policies, procedures, and processes. Upon request, reasonable accommodations in the application process can be provided to individuals with qualifying disabilities. Please contact the Human Resources Department for further information or to request an accommodation. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * What days are you available to teach? Monday/Wednesday/Friday Tuesday/Thursday Monday-Friday * What time of the day are you available to teach? Morning Afternoon Evening Anytime * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? California Lutheran University Website Cal Lutheran Careers Facebook Chronicles of Higher Ed. Monster Career Builder Higher Ed Jobs Inside Higher Ed Ventura County Star Educause LinkedIn Twitter Personal Referral Agency Referral Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Optional Documents Other Human Resources California Lutheran University 60 W. Olsen Rd. #1100 Thousand Oaks, CA 91360 Office (805) 493-3185 Fax (805) 493-3655 California Lutheran University is an Equal Opportunity Employer To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
